The code statements that lead to the bug are:
usbhs_mod_remove(priv);
usbhs_fifo_remove(priv);
usbhs_pipe_remove(priv);
Reason:
These functions free resources (including the pipe array used by the interrupt handler) while the interrupt handler is still registered, so any interrupt that occurs after these calls but before the IRQ is freed can access freed memory, causing a use-after-free.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
devm_free_irq(&pdev->dev, priv->irq, priv);
Reason:
This call disables the interrupt and synchronizes by waiting for any running ISR to complete before the resources are freed, preventing access to freed memory.

